§ `Part 2-3 Division 3 -- the work test`

#ASSERT `the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period` EQUALS 295
#ASSERT `the hours of qualifying work needed in a qualifying period` EQUALS 330
#ASSERT `the hours taken for a flexible PPL day for a previous child` EQUALS 7.6
#ASSERT `the number of days in the work test period` FALSE EQUALS 392
#ASSERT `the number of days in the work test period` TRUE EQUALS 600
-- the work test period is the 392 days immediately before 1 July 2025: 4 June 2024 to 30 June 2025
#ASSERT `the first day of the work test period` (Date 1 7 2025) 392 EQUALS Date 4 6 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of the work test period` (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS Date 30 6 2025
#ASSERT `the first day of the work test period` (Date 1 7 2025) 600 EQUALS Date 9 11 2023
-- section 33(1): subsection (2A) applies and the claimant would not satisfy the test: the work cessation day (1 Feb 2025)
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 2 2025
-- section 33(1)(b): born after the expected date of birth and would not satisfy with the period from birth: the expected date of birth
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 2 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- section 33(1)(c): otherwise, the day the child is born
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 2 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 4 2025
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 2 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS Date 1 2 2025
-- section 33(2), for an initial eligibility determination: subsection (2A) applies and the claimant would not satisfy: the work cessation day
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 2 2025
-- section 33(2)(b): otherwise the expected date of birth
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 2 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
#ASSERT `the day the work test period is counted back from` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- section 36(2): a permissible break is at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days
#ASSERT NOT `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` 0
#ASSERT `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` 1
#ASSERT `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` 84
#ASSERT NOT `the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` 85
-- section 36(3)(c): the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier (1 January 2025 plus 84 days is 26 March 2025)
#ASSERT `the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 25 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 26 3 2025)
#ASSERT NOT `the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 27 3 2025)
-- section 34(1)(a)-(b): at least one hour
#ASSERT NOT `at least one hour` 0.99
#ASSERT `at least one hour` 1
#ASSERT `at least one hour` 1.01

